 "notes": [
  "Workbook orientation: cell A5 \"Exit Station Two-Letter Code\" labels the ROW labels, i.e. sheet rows = exit station and sheet columns = entry station. Verified two ways: (1) BART July 2026 Monthly Ridership Snapshot PDF \"Ridership by Station (Average Weekday)\" equals the sheet ROW totals of Ridership_202607.xlsx (e.g. Embarcadero 22,874 vs row total 22,871; column total 20,218); (2) DataSF \"BART Daily Station Exits\" (m2xz-p7ja, BART-sourced) mean of July 2025 weekdays for Embarcadero = 19,214 vs Ridership_202507.xlsx row total 19,210 (column total 17,543). So avgWeekdayExits = sheet row totals, avgWeekdayEntries = sheet column totals. od.matrix below is TRANSPOSED from the sheet so that matrix[origin][destination].",
  "avgWeekdayExits_Aug2025 / systemAvgWeekdayTrips_Aug2025: same metric from Ridership_202508.xlsx inside https://www.bart.gov/sites/default/files/2026-02/ridership_OD_2025.zip, for year-over-year/seasonal context.",
  "Values are BART-published averages (fractional because they are monthly totals divided by number of weekdays). Rounded here to 0.1; od.matrix is rounded to 0.01.",
  "Station codes: BART reports use two-letter DAS codes (bart_station-names.xls). They were mapped by station name to BART GTFS parent_station codes (stops.txt, e.g. EM->EMBR, BK->DBRK (Downtown Berkeley), ED->DUBL, WS->WARM, BE->BERY, SO->SFIA, OA->OAKL). Mapping is in bartTwoLetterCode.",
  "sfStations* = sum over the 8 stations inside San Francisco (EMBR, MONT, POWL, CIVC, 16TH, 24TH, GLEN, BALB), summed here. Daly City/Colma are outside SF city limits.",
  "Trips are fare-gate entry/exit pairs (linked BART trips), not boardings; transfers within BART are not counted separately. August is a summer month (no university terms, some vacation) \u2014 compare with other months before treating as typical.",
  "Hourly OD data exists at https://afcweb.bart.gov/ridership/origin-destination/ (not downloaded; large files)."
 ],
